A||||4||DavidHenshaw||Fast idle||||1||
Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||05-15-2001||09:47 AM||||My 86 V6 GT automatic trans has suddunly gone from normal idle to 1900 rpm idle while in drive. What gives. Can't find much in the Haynes manual and don't want to start replacing parts unnecessairly.<P>Dave <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||84Bill||05-15-2001||09:53 AM||||Check for a vaccume leak 99% of the time its a leak.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||05-15-2001||09:59 AM||||1900 RPM in an auto is really high. Look for a big vacuum leak, like the brake booster hose fell off, or a vacuum line somewhere is completely off<P> or your gas pedal is not releaseing all the way, or your butterfly is not closed.<P>  I would worry about driving the car that way - its gotta be really slamming when you put it in drive or reverse!||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||05-15-2001||01:21 PM||||Yeah, more than likely its a vaccuum leak.<BR>For one that serious, Id go DIRECTLY to the EGR tube...I'd betcha its a gonner! Good luck! M7F||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||05-15-2001||09:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>Yeah, more than likely its a vaccuum leak.<BR>For one that serious, Id go DIRECTLY to the EGR tube...I'd betcha its a gonner! Good luck! M7F</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Exactly!<BR>Had a similar situation. Car would idle at 1500-2000 RPM. EGR tube was broken at the plenum end. Also would occasionally turn on the check engine light when I was sitting at a red light. Probably because it was idling so much higher than the ECM was telling it. <BR>Once you fix your leak, your car will idle very slowly and/or stall. It will do that until you drive it a bit, and the ECM resets the IAC.<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
